{
  "id": "22282_chikokusuru",
  "headword": "{遅刻|ちこく}する",
  "reading": "ちこくする",
  "romaji": "chikokusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to be late; to arrive late; to be tardy",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be late; to arrive late; to be tardy",
      "explanation": "To arrive after the expected or scheduled time, particularly for school, work, meetings, or appointments."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22282_chikokusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "また{遅刻|ちこく}した。",
      "english": "I was late again.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22282_chikokusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{授業|じゅぎょう}に{遅刻|ちこく}しないでください。",
      "english": "Please don't be late for class.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22282_chikokusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{電車|でんしゃ}が{遅|おく}れたせいで{会議|かいぎ}に{遅刻|ちこく}してしまった。",
      "english": "I ended up being late to the meeting because the train was delayed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22282_chikokusuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}はいつも{遅刻|ちこく}する。",
      "english": "He is always late.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers specifically to arriving after a set start time, most commonly for school, work, or formal appointments. In Japanese society, punctuality is highly valued, and {遅刻|ちこく} carries a stronger sense of social fault than the English word \"late.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {学校|がっこう}に{遅刻|ちこく}する: to be late for school\n- {会社|かいしゃ}に{遅刻|ちこく}する: to be late for work\n- {遅刻|ちこく}{届|とど}け: late arrival notice\n- {遅刻|ちこく}{常習|じょうしゅう}: habitual lateness\n- {遅刻|ちこく}ぎりぎり: barely on time / cutting it close\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {遅|おく}れる: to be late — more general; can describe delays of any kind, not just arriving late to a scheduled event\n- {間|ま}に{合|あ}わない: to not make it in time — focuses on missing a deadline rather than arriving late to a place",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
